  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760277,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 19740417 - 25 Years Lion: A Commodore 64 Adventure\n\nTwenty-five years have passed since the chilling events of *1984*. Oceania remains, its grip on society tighter than ever. *19740417 - 25 Years Lion* plunges you into the role of Elias, a young man haunted by fragmented memories and a growing suspicion that the Party’s narrative isn’t the whole truth. \n\nThis atmospheric adventure for the Commodore 64 blends exploration, puzzle-solving, and tense stealth sequences. Navigate the decaying remnants of London, now a sprawling, oppressive metropolis, uncovering clues about a hidden resistance movement known as \"The Lions.\"  \n\nGameplay revolves around gathering information, avoiding the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police, and deciphering cryptic messages left by previous rebels.  Utilize Elias’s limited resources – a rusty wrench, a flickering flashlight, and his wits – to overcome obstacles and expose the Party’s lies.  The game features a haunting soundtrack and pixel-perfect graphics that evoke the bleakness and paranoia of Orwell’s dystopian vision. Can you uncover the truth and reignite the flame of rebellion?"
    },
